(*
DebugProbeC6 — rete#311: a program with TIMERS, held at a breakpoint on a board.

ReadLineProbe showed a VM blocked in `readLine` is left alone by the observer — but it
declared no timers, so nothing was judging it. This one is judged: a 1 s repeating timer
and `appLiveness: 8000`, the same shape as WedgeProbeC6, so a VM held longer than 8 s at a
breakpoint is exactly what the observer rebooted a wedged node for. The claim under test
is that a HELD VM is not a WEDGED one (observer_core.h §3.2, `held`).

Each tick calls `countTo:` — a method with a loop and a local, the same shape as the
host gate's 46_debug_target.nsl — so there is something to break in, step through and
inspect. The line it prints carries the tick number and the sum so a hold is visible as
a gap in the timestamps and a step is visible as the same tick finishing late.

Needs the hooks build: OEVM_DEBUG_HOOKS=1 (zephyr/CMakeLists.txt) — the production
image compiles the breakpoint checks out AND answers platform_debug_enabled() = 0, so
on it this probe just ticks.
Run: OEVM_DEBUG_HOOKS=1 run.sh --node DebugProbeC6.nsl
(prj_esp32c6.conf carries the interrupt-driven UART every C6 image needs; the polled
reader hangs the board, and the ISR is what lets `dbg:pause` stop a running tick.)
*)
class DebugProbeC6 packageUsing: manifest = (
  | plat space timers tickCh ticks ::= 0. |
) (

  public main: platform args: args = (
    plat:: platform.
    space:: plat space.
    timers:: plat timers.
    space whenever: 'sys/timer' do: [ :e | timers dispatch: e ].

    tickCh:: space channel: 'probe/tick'.
    tickCh whenever: '' do: [ :m | self tick ].
    timers every: 1000 post: #t on: tickCh.
    (* No bridge here, so the probe declares its own cadence: 1000 x 8, the deadline
       wedge-detect reports. Undeclared means NOT JUDGED, which would prove nothing. *)
    plat appLiveness: 8000.
    'dbg-probe: ticking' println.

    [ true ] whileTrue: [ plat pumpEvents. space drain ].
    ^ self )

  tick = (
    | sum |
    ticks:: ticks + 1.
    sum:: self countTo: ticks.
    ('dbg-probe tick ' , ticks printString , ' sum ' , sum printString) println.
    ^ self )

  (* The breakpoint target: a loop and a local, as in 46_debug_target.nsl. *)
  countTo: n = (
    | sum |
    sum:: 0.
    1 to: n do: [ :i | sum:: sum + i ].
    ^ sum )

) : (
)
